This extension adds inZOI modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Installs mods with a "mod_manifest.json" manifest to the "DOCUMENTS\inZOI\Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with both a "Content" and a "Binaries" folder to the "BlueClient" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a "LogicMods" folder to the "BlueClient\Content\Paks\LogicMods" folder.[/*]
[*]Creations mods are installed to the "CREATIONS_PATH" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a ".pak" file to the "BlueClient\Content\Paks\~mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Aigenerated mods are recognised by the Aigenerated installer.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a "dwmapi.dll" file to the "BlueClient\Binaries\Win64" folder.[/*]
[*]Canvas mods are recognised by the Canvas installer.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named "dsound.dll" and a file or folder named "sig.lua".[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a ".lua" file and a "Scripts" folder to the "BlueClient\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named "appearance.dat", a file or folder named "motion.dat", a file or folder named "albedo.jpg", a file with the ".glb" extension, a file with the ".dat" extension and a file with one of these extensions: ".glb" or ".dat".[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a ".dll" file and a "dlls" folder to the "BlueClient\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Animations mods are recognised by the Animations installer.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a top-level folder such as "BlueClient", "Engine" or "Content" to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Myappearances mods are recognised by the Myappearances installer.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a config file such as "engine.ini" or "game.ini".[/*]
[*]Textures mods are recognised by the Textures installer.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a ".sav" file.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with anything unrecognised with no pak file to the "BlueClient\Binaries\Win64" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

